# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets — _headers
# Served from the assets root (wrangler.jsonc: assets.directory = "./dist").
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# SEMANTICS NOTE: rules are CUMULATIVE. A request matching several path
# patterns inherits every matched rule's headers, and a header set twice is
# JOINED with a comma (not overridden). The Cache-Control paths below are kept
# mutually exclusive so no asset ever receives two DIFFERENT ones.
#
# The one deliberate exception is /*.html vs /ru/*.html. `*` spans segments, so
# the first already covers the second — but _headers is fail-open, a pattern
# that quietly stops matching costs a wrong Cache-Control with no error
# anywhere, and routing added a whole second tree that every rule here predates.
# Both carry the SAME value, so the worst case is `no-cache, no-cache`.

# --- Security headers (site-wide, unique header names) ---
#
# The CSP ships now that both of its blockers are gone: there are no inline
# style attributes left anywhere, and the one inline <script> (the
# false-friends redirect) died with locale routing. Everything the pages load
# is same-origin: one stylesheet, two scripts, twelve local woff2 subsets.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

# --- Fonts: content-stable woff2 subsets (and their OFL licences).
#     Large files, never change under a stable path. ---
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# --- CSS / JS: content-hashed filenames, so a deploy publishes new names
#     rather than new bytes under old ones. Never revalidated. Every asset is
#     hashed, including the render-blocking theme-init, so these patterns stay
#     mutually exclusive — see the SEMANTICS NOTE above. ---
/assets/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# --- HTML: always revalidate; never long-cache a document. Routing added a
#     whole second tree, so /ru/ is spelled out — a pattern that quietly stops
#     matching would cost a wrong Cache-Control with no error anywhere. ---
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/ru/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/ru/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
